From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 2026 21:09:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/matroskadec: export the editions and their chapters

A Matroska file can carry several editions (a theatrical and an extended
cut, for example), each with its own chapters; in an ordered edition the
chapters are the parts of the file that play, in that order. The demuxer
read every ChapterAtom into one list and threw the edition away, so a
player could not offer the editions nor play an ordered one.

Keep each EditionEntry with its flags (EditionUID, EditionFlagDefault,
EditionFlagHidden, EditionFlagOrdered) and its name (EditionString, or
the TITLE of a tag whose TagEditionUID targets it), and each top-level
chapter with ChapterFlagHidden, ChapterFlagEnabled and ChapterSegmentUUID;
read the SegmentUUID of the file. All of it is exported, as it is in the
file, in the new read-only "editions" option of the demuxer, an
AVDictionary that av_opt_get_dict_val() returns:

  count, segment_uid (hex, if any)
  N.uid N.default N.hidden N.ordered N.chapters N.name (if any)
  N.M.start N.M.end (ns; no end if the file has none) N.M.uid N.M.hidden
  N.M.enabled N.M.segment_uid (hex, if the chapter names a segment)
  N.M.title (if any)

Nothing that is demuxed changes. The AVChapters are made from the chapters
of all editions in the order of the file, with the same rule as before
(a chapter is kept only if it starts after the last one kept), so they are
the same; tags that target a chapter still go to that AVChapter; a tag that
targets only an edition still goes to the file's metadata, as before; no
key is added to any metadata, and packets and seeking are untouched.
Choosing an edition, and how to play it, is left to the player.

The element IDs are those of RFC 9559 (EditionDisplay 0x4520,
EditionString 0x4521, EditionLanguageIETF 0x45E4, ChapterSegmentUUID
0x6E67, TagEditionUID 0x63C9). Nested ChapterAtoms are still not read.

An earlier take on editions in the Matroska demuxer, by Sebastiii for
CoreELEC (an "edition" option that limits and rebases the timeline to the
selected edition), was read; this export does not change the timeline.
